{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"runty-effectible-bluewhale","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe RCA for tekite-fleece-hake found the same tracker-parent-as-code-root assumption in `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py::code_root_for`. `attach_commits` reaches it through `_lib_mutations.py`; with an absolute `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` outside the code checkout, valid code commit SHAs may be checked against the tracker parent and rejected. This is a confirmed construct/call path but was not dynamically reproduced during the bounded close-precheck investigation.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce attach-commits with a real code repo and independently relocated ticket store.\n- Confirm or reject tracker-parent root derivation as the mechanism.\n- If confirmed, add a real-git RED oracle, resolve code root from explicit/current repository context while retaining tracker reads, and perform mutation plus parity sweeps.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic experiment confirms or rejects the reported root-conflation mechanism.\n- [ ] If confirmed, valid code commits are accepted with an out-of-worktree tracker and unknown SHAs remain rejected.\n- [ ] Default in-repo tracker behavior remains green.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, and typecheck pass.","id":"9918-a5d6-8fb5-42e8","parent_id":"57b6-90b7-87bb-45e7","priority":2,"tags":["cli","git","tracker"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Resolve attach-commits code root independently from relocated tracker storage"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787025712617194001,"uuid":"be2573db-f634-4590-801c-5e07008d6024"}